{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Observation\nThe first recorded failure was Group04's comment-only review push: Gerrit rejected commit 83129b25017591d11c666463ee702ce73e2fbf5b with Missing blob 490430b52a0e274b2d9b73fb3aba1918b107543a. That push later succeeded unchanged without an object-store repair. Subsequent comment-only pushes intermittently failed on historical tests tree 37cf50101b30d7d6cf08f391ad13144ee2fd3183 while other pushes succeeded.\n\nGroup15 reproduced the tree rejection on both an old-base candidate and a fresh-origin/main candidate. The named tree is reachable from Gerrit main and readable inside the Gerrit container as uid 1000. Full container fsck --full --connectivity-only --no-dangling --strict exits 0. The Gerrit receive stack throws from JGit FullConnectivityChecker.checkObjects:196 while checking an incoming pack's external delta base. Git 2.56's HTTPS helper still invokes send-pack --thin for git push --no-thin. A local no-delta pack of the exact candidate indexed self-contained; one controlled push with pack.window=0 and pack.depth=0 succeeded unchanged as Gerrit 3084. The exact reason JGit fails to mark that historical base reachable remains unproven. Evidence and command IDs are in the ticket comments.\n\n## Investigation and recovery plan\n1. Preserve the accepted no-delta client packing workaround for currently blocked review uploads without changing Gerrit objects, live refs, or commit content.\n2. Compare the incoming pack's external bases with Gerrit's advertised haves and JGit's reachability walk on an isolated reproduction using the deployed Gerrit/JGit version. Identify why a readable main-history object is not marked reachable.\n3. Correct the verified failure mechanism in the smallest reversible place. If server object-store mutation is ever justified, take the EBS snapshot and follow infra/runbooks/gerrit-object-store-repair.md first; the present fsck/readability evidence does not justify that repair.\n4. Verify the fix with an ordinary HTTPS review push, full repository connectivity, and replication/merged-reachability checks. Record the exact revision and CI outcome.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Given a historical tree reachable from Gerrit main, when a review pack uses it as an external delta base, then Gerrit either accepts a valid pack or reports a concrete integrity defect rather than incorrectly treating the readable tree as missing.\n- Given the confirmed correction or configured client workaround, when an ordinary review upload follows the documented contribution path, then it creates a Gerrit change for the exact reviewed revision and its normal LLM-Review and Verified gates run.\n- Given recovery checks, full fsck, replication, and 50 recent merged-revision reachability pass without moving main backward.\n- Record the mechanism, reproduction, correction, and push/CI evidence before closing this bug.","title":"Investigate Gerrit thin-pack connectivity rejection of readable objects"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1792796435292560392,"uuid":"90ccc84b-d0dd-4a78-a7b5-f3b5bdcae383"}